Before you push to Git
Create a .gitignore file to prevent local credentials, logs, and backup data from being committed:


gitignore
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.env
*.xlsx
logs/
*.log
This excludes all Excel files; if you intend to commit a sanitized sample inventory, use a sample file with fake credentials and adjust the ignore rule accordingly.

Then commit the documentation and code:


bash
git add README.md requirements.txt cisco_backup.py .gitignore
git commit -m "Add automated Cisco configuration backup"
git push
